# Hydraulics 101's own components. Sandbox.qml is the entry and is loaded by URL, so
# it is deliberately not listed - everything it refers to by bare type name is.
#
# This file exists because the lab is also published, and launches full-screen
# from /labs/run/?lab=hydraulics-101. A directory import resolves by LISTING the
# directory, and a directory cannot be listed over HTTP - so without this
# manifest every sibling type silently stops existing in the browser while
# still working on the desktop ("MyPanel is not a type").
#
# Nothing to list yet. Add a line the moment you split a component out of
# Sandbox.qml:
#
#     MyPanel 1.0 MyPanel.qml
#
# Comments here start with '#'. A '//' comment fails the whole file to parse,
# and the error surfaces on the import line instead, which sends you looking
# in the wrong place entirely.
